<title>POLAND: Polifarbs pick merger adviser.</title>
<headline>Polifarbs pick merger adviser.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's two leading paintmakers Polifarb Cieszyn and Polifarb Wroclaw picked Boston Consulting Group to advise them on the planned merger, Polifarb Wroclaw said in a statement on Thursday.</p>
<p>The company said the advisor would prepare an outline for the two firm's integration including the proposed new organisational structure and new ways of its operation.</p>
<p>The two Polifarbs annouced their plan to merge in December and said the operation could take place early in the second half of 1997 at the earliest.</p>
<p>The statement said the consulting firm would also coordinate and monitor the integration of the two companie's operations and advise both firms during and after the merger.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
